WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.225 line:0
It starts with a brief.

2
00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:04.108 line:0
It ends with a film.

3
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.377 line:0
In between, everything lives in one folder.

4
00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:11.908 line:0
The brief, the storyboard, the script, the timings:

5
00:00:11.941 --> 00:00:14.518 line:0
every decision is written to a file.

6
00:00:14.518 --> 00:00:17.364 line:0
So a film can be reviewed like code.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.689 line:0
Six specialist agents share the work.

8
00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:22.512 line:0
The script comes first:

9
00:00:22.512 --> 00:00:26.958 line:0
a person approves the angle and the words before anything is recorded.

10
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:30.118 line:0
The storyboard then acts as the contract.

11
00:00:30.209 --> 00:00:34.110 line:0
Scenes, voice and sound move forward at the same time,

12
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.236 line:0
each in its own files.

13
00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:38.336 line:0
The last agent wrote none of it:

14
00:00:38.336 --> 00:00:40.788 line:0
it only looks at the rendered film.

15
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.100 line:0
Once the film is rendered,

16
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.480 line:0
the factory measures what can be measured:

17
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.222 line:0
format, duration, loudness.

18
00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:50.614 line:0
It never says the film is good.

19
00:00:50.647 --> 00:00:54.840 line:0
Watching it and listening to it is still someone's job.

20
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.796 line:0
That is how a brief becomes a film you can check.
